<title>USA: Integrated Tech adopts holders' rights plan.</title>
<headline>Integrated Tech adopts holders' rights plan.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Integrated Technology USA Inc said Thursday that it adopted a stockholders' rights plan in which common stock purchase rights will be distributed as a dividend at the rate of one right for each share of common stock.</p>
<p>The company said the rights will expire on July 23, 2007.</p>
<p>Each right will entitle stockholders to buy one quarter of a share of common stock for $1.50, the company said.</p>
<p>The rights will be exercisable only if a person or group acquires 15 percent or more of the company's common stock, the company said.</p>
</text>
